---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';import Playground from '../../components/Playground';import studies from '../../data/studies.json';
export function getStaticPaths(){return studies.map(study=>({params:{slug:study.scene},props:{study}}))}
const {study}=Astro.props;
const fields=Object.values(study.schemas)[0];
const titles:Record<string,string>={device:"3D Phone Product Demo",castle:"3D Castle Animation",dragon:"Skeletal Dragon Animation",underwater:"Underwater Train Animation",unet:"U-Net Scientific Explainer",grain:"Grain Film Animation",warehouse:"Isometric Logistics Animation",paper:"Paper Stop-Motion Animation",storybook:"Storybook Collage Animation",ink:"Ink Drawing Animation",showreel:"Kinetic Typography",evolution:"Product Evolution Animation"};
---
<Page title={`${titles[study.scene]} Playground — EditableFrame`} description={study.detail} path={`/genres/${study.scene}/`}>
<section class="hero genre-hero"><a class="back-link" href="/#gallery">← Back to the collection</a><p class="eyebrow">{study.genre} / EDITABLE CODE STUDY</p><h1>{study.hook}</h1><p class="genre-intro">{study.detail}</p></section><div class="studio-wrap"><Playground initial={study.scene} client:visible/></div><section class="section genre-notes"><div><span class="eyebrow">MAKE IT YOURS</span><h2>Small controls.<br/>A different feeling.</h2></div><div><p>This {study.duration}-second study uses drawing code and 3D rendering, with credited GLB assets in the product demo. Its original title is <em>{study.title}</em>. Start the preview, try the controls, then scrub to compare the same moment before and after an edit.</p><ul>{Object.values(fields).map((f:any)=><li>{f.label}</li>)}</ul><p>Changes are reversible and saved in this browser. Download a still or an edit recipe; an edit recipe is a playground settings file, not a finished video.</p><a class="text-link" href="/guide/">Learn about code-generated video and the beta SDK ↗</a></div></section><section class="section related"><h2>Take a different direction.</h2><div class="gallery-grid">{studies.filter(s=>s.scene!==study.scene).slice(0,3).map(s=><a class="study-card" href={`/genres/${s.scene}/`}><img src={`/demos/${s.scene}.jpg`} alt={s.title} width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy"/><span class="eyebrow">{s.genre}</span><h3>{s.title}</h3></a>)}</div></section>
</Page>
